==============================================================================
Dig-the-f-up is a Rust port of DigUp (https://github.com/ARahim3/DigUp) by Abdur Rahim, released under the MIT
License. Its MIT copyright and permission notice is reproduced in full below and must stay with any redistribution
of this code.

The on-disk index schema (version 5), search scoring, prompts and indexing constants are taken from that project's
Swift sources so that indexes and search quality stay comparable.

Other components: llama.cpp b11461 (MIT, compiled into the app; notice below). FFmpeg 7.1.5 (LGPL-2.1-or-later;
ffmpeg and ffprobe, bundled as separate programs in release packages). pdfium (BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0; bundled in
Windows and Linux packages, licence in LICENSE-pdfium.txt). Full component list and Rust crate licenses:
docs/THIRD-PARTY.md and scripts/gen-third-party-licenses.sh.

Models (not shipped in the app, downloaded at run time from pinned Hugging Face revisions):

- EmbeddingGemma 2 by Google DeepMind (https://huggingface.co/google/embeddinggemma-2), Apache License 2.0 per its
  model card and the card of the GGUF conversion used (https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/embeddinggemma-2-GGUF,
  pinned revision in crates/dtfu-models); checked 2026-10-12.
- Optional OCR engine (cargo feature `lighton` of dtfu-ocr): LightOnOCR-3-0.8B by LightOn
  (https://huggingface.co/lightonai/LightOnOCR-3-0.8B), via the community GGUF conversion by mradermacher
  (https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/LightOnOCR-3-0.8B-GGUF, pinned revision in crates/dtfu-models), whose GGUF
  metadata declares `general.license = apache-2.0`; both model cards say Apache License 2.0 (checked 2026-10-12). Ship
  the licence text next to the model files if they are ever redistributed.

